kitty for Debian/Ubuntu (deb.griffo.io)
=======================================

This package ships the official upstream prebuilt bundle, unmodified, under
/opt/kitty: its own Python runtime, its own copies of harfbuzz, freetype,
cairo, OpenSSL and friends. /usr/bin/kitty and /usr/bin/kitten are symlinks
into it. The desktop entry, icons, man pages, terminfo and shell integration
files live at the same paths Debian's own packages use.

Shell completions
-----------------
fish and zsh completions for kitty, kitten and clone-in-kitty are installed
system-wide (they call `kitten __complete__` at completion time). bash has
no static completion file: kitty's shell integration enables it, or run
    source <(kitten __complete__ setup bash)

Remote machines
---------------
Install only kitty-terminfo on hosts you ssh into so TERM=xterm-kitty is
known there, or let the ssh kitten copy it for you.

kitten update-self
------------------
`kitten update-self` downloads a new kitten binary over the one it is run
from, which is the packaged /opt/kitty/bin/kitten. Do not use it; upgrade
with apt instead. If you did run it, `apt reinstall kitty` restores the
packaged binary.

Opening files and URLs with kitty
---------------------------------
Like Debian, kitty-open.desktop is not installed live because it registers
kitty as a handler for text/*, image/*, directories and ssh URLs, which can
make it the default opener where none is set. To opt in:
    cp /usr/share/doc/kitty/examples/kitty-open.desktop ~/.local/share/applications/

Input method support
--------------------
To type non-Latin characters through ibus or fcitx5, start kitty with
    GLFW_IM_MODULE=ibus kitty
(fcitx5 speaks the ibus protocol, so "ibus" is correct for it too).
